  "question": {
    "text": "The distance between object and its two times magnified real image as produced by a convex lens is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The focal length of the lens used is ________<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Magnification, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>u</mi><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>As,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>From lens equation, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}